From fab4608eac4ba7fe6f0b01b67dcaf97aad4fca19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:58:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(review): pin the capped downsample in raster space

The 5:1 leg probed grim's default logical-size capture, a 1.25x linear
upscale of the framebuffer at scale 0.8, so its expected values encoded
the upscale's phase and matched no sampling model. Capture the
framebuffer 1:1 with grim -s 0.8, assert the raster rect (32,32,320,240)
by its black edges, and pin px 41/42 = (0,159,96)/(0,96,159) from the tap
grid: ratio 5.0, four taps at 1.25-texel steps over the alternating
columns. The one-texel-step mutation now fails the cap leg at the
behavioural assert with the even mix (0,128,128) at both pixels.

Document that wlr_scene_set_downsample_mode defaults to bilinear in the
library while the shell sets box from appearance.downsample.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 tests/harness/checks/render/downsample_box.sh | 28 +++++++++++++++----
 umbrielfx/include/umbrielfx/types/wlr_scene.h |  3 +-
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/harness/checks/render/downsample_box.sh b/tests/harness/checks/render/downsample_box.sh
